!!! The .nilhtml template engine.
!!!
!!! Tags are NyWeb's, because they are good tags and because anyone moving a
!!! page over should not have to relearn them:
!!!
!!!   <%= name %>                 a value, HTML-escaped
!!!   <%! name %>                 a value, raw — see the warning on raw-output
!!!   <%# anything %>             a comment, dropped
!!!   <% if name %> … <% end %>   a section, taken when the name is set
!!!   <% if name %> … <% else %> … <% end %>
!!!   <% unless name %> … <% end %>
!!!   <% for one in many %> … <% end %>   repeats, binding one.field
!!!   <%@ include "partial.nilhtml" %>
!!!   <%@ layout "layouts/main.nilhtml" %>
!!!   <%@ content %>              in a layout: where the page goes
!!!
!!! What the tags no longer hold is Ny code. NyWeb's engine parsed expressions
!!! and the runtime evaluated them; here a tag names something the handler
!!! published and nothing else. See nilweb.template.context for why that is a
!!! feature rather than a shortfall.
!!!
!!! The source is tokenised once and rendered start-at the token array, rather
!!! than rescanned for every nested block. A page with a loop inside a
!!! conditional inside a layout would otherwise walk its own text four times.

book nilweb.template.render

read nil.std.core
read nil.std.io.file
read nil.std.text
read everything from nilweb.text.scan
read everything from nilweb.template.context


!!! How many includes and layouts deep a render may go before it is judged to
!!! be a cycle. A page that legitimately nests ten layouts does not exist; a
!!! partial that includes itself does, and without this it takes the process.
constant nesting-limit as number is 10


public template-token begin record
    !!! literal, output, raw, comment, if, unless, else, ending, loop,
    !!! include, layout, slot, broken
    field kind as text
    field body as text
end record


public render-result begin record
    field text-out as text
    field rendered as boolean
    field complaint as text
end record


!!! --- Escape text for HTML content and double-quoted attributes.
!!!
!!! Five characters, in this order — ampersand first, or the escapes this
!!! introduces are escaped again and `&lt;` reaches the page as `&amp;lt;`.
!!! The apostrophe is included because an attribute may be single-quoted, and
!!! a framework that only escaped the double quote would be one where the
!!! difference between quote styles is a vulnerability.

public escape-html receives raw as text returns text begin paragraph
    variable out as text is raw
    set out to nil.std.text::replace with s being out, old_value being "&", new_value being "&amp;"
    set out to nil.std.text::replace with s being out, old_value being "<", new_value being "&lt;"
    set out to nil.std.text::replace with s being out, old_value being ">", new_value being "&gt;"
    set out to nil.std.text::replace with s being out, old_value being quote, new_value being "&quot;"
    set out to nil.std.text::replace with s being out, old_value being "'", new_value being "&#39;"
    give out
end paragraph


!!! --- Break a template into literal runs and tags.
!!!
!!! An unterminated `<%` is a `broken` token rather than a silent truncation,
!!! so a missing `%>` is reported with the template rather than discovered as
!!! a half-rendered page.

public tokenize receives source as text returns array of template-token begin paragraph
    variable tokens as array of template-token is []
    variable rest as text is source
    repeat forever
        value opened is nil.std.text::index_of with s being rest, needle being "<%"
        when opened is less than 0 then
            when not (rest equals "") then
                append build template-token with kind being "literal", body being rest to tokens
            end when
            stop repeating
        end when
        when opened is greater than 0 then
            append build template-token with kind being "literal",
                body being (nil.std.text::substring with s being rest, start being 0, length being opened) to tokens
        end when
        value after-open is nil.std.text::substring with s being rest, start being opened plus 2,
            length being (nil.std.text::length with s being rest) minus opened minus 2
        value closed is nil.std.text::index_of with s being after-open, needle being "%>"
        when closed is less than 0 then
            append build template-token with kind being "broken", body being after-open to tokens
            stop repeating
        end when
        value inside is nil.std.text::substring with s being after-open, start being 0, length being closed
        append (classify with inside being inside) to tokens
        set rest to nil.std.text::substring with s being after-open, start being closed plus 2,
            length being (nil.std.text::length with s being after-open) minus closed minus 2
    end repeat
    give tokens
end paragraph


classify receives inside as text returns template-token begin paragraph
    when inside equals "" then
        give build template-token with kind being "comment", body being ""
    end when
    value marker is nil.std.text::substring with s being inside, start being 0, length being 1
    value rest is nil.std.text::trim with s being
        (nil.std.text::substring with s being inside, start being 1,
            length being (nil.std.text::length with s being inside) minus 1)

    when marker equals "=" then
        give build template-token with kind being "output", body being rest
    end when
    when marker equals "!" then
        give build template-token with kind being "raw", body being rest
    end when
    when marker equals "#" then
        give build template-token with kind being "comment", body being rest
    end when
    when marker equals "@" then
        give classify-directive with rest being rest
    end when

    value word-run is nil.std.text::trim with s being inside
    value first-word is before-first with input being word-run, separator being " "
    value tail is nil.std.text::trim with s being (after-first with input being word-run, separator being " ")
    when first-word equals "if" then
        give build template-token with kind being "if", body being tail
    end when
    when first-word equals "unless" then
        give build template-token with kind being "unless", body being tail
    end when
    when first-word equals "for" then
        give build template-token with kind being "loop", body being tail
    end when
    when word-run equals "else" then
        give build template-token with kind being "else", body being ""
    end when
    when word-run equals "end" then
        give build template-token with kind being "ending", body being ""
    end when
    give build template-token with kind being "broken", body being word-run
end paragraph


classify-directive receives rest as text returns template-token begin paragraph
    value word-run is nil.std.text::trim with s being rest
    value first-word is before-first with input being word-run, separator being " "
    value named is unquoted with raw being (nil.std.text::trim with s being
        (after-first with input being word-run, separator being " "))
    when first-word equals "include" then
        give build template-token with kind being "include", body being named
    end when
    when first-word equals "layout" then
        give build template-token with kind being "layout", body being named
    end when
    when word-run equals "content" then
        give build template-token with kind being "slot", body being ""
    end when
    give build template-token with kind being "broken", body being word-run
end paragraph


unquoted receives raw as text returns text begin paragraph
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being raw
    when width is less than 2 then
        give raw
    end when
    value first is nil.std.text::substring with s being raw, start being 0, length being 1
    value last is nil.std.text::substring with s being raw, start being width minus 1, length being 1
    when first equals quote and last equals quote then
        give nil.std.text::substring with s being raw, start being 1, length being width minus 2
    end when
    give raw
end paragraph


!!! --- The compiled-template cache.
!!!
!!! Rendering a page meant reading three files and tokenising all of them, on
!!! every request: measured on the demonstration application, a templated page
!!! served at half the rate of one that returned plain text, and the whole of
!!! that difference was this.
!!!
!!! Keyed by path and validated against the file's modification time, so a
!!! template edited while the server runs is picked up without a restart and
!!! an unchanged one costs a timestamp check rather than a read and a parse.
!!! That is why nil.std.io grew `modified_at`: without it a cache cannot tell
!!! whether what it holds is current except by re-reading the file, which is
!!! the thing the cache exists to avoid.

cached-template begin record
    field path as text
    field tokens as array of template-token
    field layout as text
    field stamped-at as number
    field live as boolean
end record


public variable cache-store as array of cached-template is []

!!! Whether to trust the cache without checking the file's timestamp.
!!!
!!! Off by default, because a template edited during development that does not
!!! appear is a confusing minute. On, a page costs no filesystem call at all,
!!! which is what a server fronting unchanging templates wants.
public variable cache-is-frozen as boolean is false


public freeze-cache receives frozen as boolean returns nothing begin paragraph
    set nilweb.template.render::cache-is-frozen to frozen
    give nothing
end paragraph


public clear-cache returns nothing begin paragraph
    variable empty as array of cached-template is []
    set nilweb.template.render::cache-store to empty
    give nothing
end paragraph


public cached-count returns number begin paragraph
    variable total as number is 0
    repeat for each one in nilweb.template.render::cache-store
        when one.live then
            set total to total plus 1
        end when
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph


stamp-of receives path as text returns number begin paragraph
    value found is nil.std.io::modified_at with path being path
    consider found
        when Result.Ok holding stamped then give stamped
        otherwise give 0 minus 1
    end consider
end paragraph


cache-slot-of receives path as text returns number begin paragraph
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of nilweb.template.render::cache-store
        value one is nilweb.template.render::cache-store at index
        when one.live and one.path equals path then
            give index
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give 0 minus 1
end paragraph


!!! --- The tokens for a template, from the cache when they are current.

public prepared begin record
    field tokens as array of template-token
    field layout as text
    field ready as boolean
    field complaint as text
end record


public prepare receives name as text, root as text returns prepared begin paragraph
    variable none-yet as array of template-token is []
    value guarded is guard-name with name being name
    when not (guarded equals "") then
        give build prepared with tokens being none-yet, layout being "", ready being false,
            complaint being guarded
    end when
    value path is when root equals "" give name otherwise give root plus "/" plus name end when

    value slot is cache-slot-of with path being path
    when slot is at least 0 then
        value held is nilweb.template.render::cache-store at slot
        value still-good is nilweb.template.render::cache-is-frozen
            or (stamp-of with path being path) equals held.stamped-at
        when still-good then
            give build prepared with tokens being held.tokens, layout being held.layout,
                ready being true, complaint being ""
        end when
    end when

    value loaded is load-template with name being name, root being root
    when not loaded.rendered then
        give build prepared with tokens being none-yet, layout being "", ready being false,
            complaint being loaded.complaint
    end when
    value tokens is tokenize with source being loaded.text-out
    value layout is first-layout with tokens being tokens
    value fresh is build cached-template with path being path, tokens being tokens,
        layout being layout, stamped-at being (stamp-of with path being path), live being true
    when slot is at least 0 then
        set nilweb.template.render::cache-store at slot to fresh
    otherwise
        append fresh to nilweb.template.render::cache-store
    end when
    give build prepared with tokens being tokens, layout being layout, ready being true,
        complaint being ""
end paragraph


!!! --- Render a template held as text.

public render-source receives source as text, page-data as render-context, root as text
    returns render-result begin paragraph
    give render-at-depth with source being source, page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being 0
end paragraph


!!! --- Render a template held in a file under `root`.

public render-file receives name as text, page-data as render-context, root as text
    returns render-result begin paragraph
    give render-cached with name being name, page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being 0
end paragraph


!!! --- Render a template from the cache, including its layout and includes.
!!!
!!! The same walk as render-at-depth, but starting from tokens that were
!!! already parsed rather than from text that has to be. A page with a layout
!!! and a partial costs three timestamp checks instead of three reads and
!!! three parses.

render-cached receives name as text, page-data as render-context, root as text, depth as number
    returns render-result begin paragraph
    when depth is greater than nesting-limit then
        give failed-render with complaint being "templates nest more than "
            plus (nesting-limit becomes text) plus " deep; this is a cycle"
    end when
    value ready is prepare with name being name, root being root
    when not ready.ready then
        give failed-render with complaint being ready.complaint
    end when

    value inner is render-range with tokens being ready.tokens, start-at being 0,
        upto being the length of ready.tokens, page-data being page-data, root being root,
        depth being depth
    when not inner.rendered then
        give inner
    end when
    when ready.layout equals "" then
        give inner
    end when

    value shell is prepare with name being ready.layout, root being root
    when not shell.ready then
        give failed-render with complaint being shell.complaint
    end when
    give render-with-slot with tokens being shell.tokens, inner being inner.text-out,
        page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth plus 1
end paragraph


!!! --- Render a layout, dropping the page in at its content slot.
!!!
!!! The page's output is placed where the slot is rather than spliced into the
!!! layout's text beforehand, which is what lets the layout stay parsed in the
!!! cache. It also means the page's output is never rescanned for tags it does
!!! not contain.
!!!
!!! Rendered as two ranges around the slot, not token by token. Token by token
!!! was the first version and it was wrong: a `<% if %>` in a layout spans
!!! several tokens, and rendering one of them alone finds no `<% end %>` and
!!! reports an unclosed block in a layout that is perfectly well formed.

!!! --- Render a template held as text, which is what render-source is for.
!!!
!!! Text rather than a cached path, so it takes the slower route: tokenise,
!!! render, and splice a layout if one is named. Used by tests and by anything
!!! holding a template it did not read from a file. A page served from disk
!!! goes through render-cached instead.

render-at-depth receives source as text, page-data as render-context, root as text, depth as number
    returns render-result begin paragraph
    when depth is greater than nesting-limit then
        give failed-render with complaint being "templates nest more than "
            plus (nesting-limit becomes text) plus " deep; this is a cycle"
    end when

    value tokens is tokenize with source being source
    value inner is render-range with tokens being tokens, start-at being 0, upto being the length of tokens,
        page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth
    when not inner.rendered then
        give inner
    end when

    value wrapper is first-layout with tokens being tokens
    when wrapper equals "" then
        give inner
    end when
    value shell is prepare with name being wrapper, root being root
    when not shell.ready then
        give failed-render with complaint being shell.complaint
    end when
    give render-with-slot with tokens being shell.tokens, inner being inner.text-out,
        page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth plus 1
end paragraph


!!! --- The layout a token list names, or "" when it names none.

first-layout receives tokens as array of template-token returns text begin paragraph
    repeat for each token in tokens
        when token.kind equals "layout" then
            give token.body
        end when
    end repeat
    give ""
end paragraph


render-with-slot receives tokens as array of template-token, inner as text,
    page-data as render-context, root as text, depth as number returns render-result begin paragraph
    when depth is greater than nesting-limit then
        give failed-render with complaint being "templates nest more than "
            plus (nesting-limit becomes text) plus " deep; this is a cycle"
    end when

    value total is the length of tokens
    value slot is slot-index-of with tokens being tokens
    when slot is less than 0 then
        !!! A layout with no content slot swallows the page. Reported rather
        !!! than rendered, because a layout that silently discards what it was
        !!! wrapping is a blank page with no explanation.
        give failed-render with complaint being
            "a layout must contain <%@ content %>, and this one does not"
    end when

    value before is render-range with tokens being tokens, start-at being 0, upto being slot,
        page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth
    when not before.rendered then
        give before
    end when
    value after is render-range with tokens being tokens, start-at being slot plus 1, upto being total,
        page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth
    when not after.rendered then
        give after
    end when
    give build render-result with text-out being before.text-out plus inner plus after.text-out,
        rendered being true, complaint being ""
end paragraph


slot-index-of receives tokens as array of template-token returns number begin paragraph
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than the length of tokens
        when (tokens at index).kind equals "slot" then
            give index
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give 0 minus 1
end paragraph


render-range receives tokens as array of template-token, start-at as number, upto as number,
    page-data as render-context, root as text, depth as number returns render-result begin paragraph
    variable out as text is ""
    variable index as number is start-at
    repeat while index is less than upto
        value token is tokens at index
        value kind is token.kind

        when kind equals "literal" then
            set out to out plus token.body
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "output" then
            set out to out plus (escape-html with raw being (value-of with page-data being page-data, name being token.body))
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "raw" then
            set out to out plus (value-of with page-data being page-data, name being token.body)
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "comment" or kind equals "layout" then
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "slot" then
            !!! Only meaningful inside a layout, where it was already filled.
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "include" then
            value done is render-cached with name being token.body, page-data being page-data,
                root being root, depth being depth plus 1
            when not done.rendered then
                give done
            end when
            set out to out plus done.text-out
            set index to index plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "if" or kind equals "unless" then
            value spans is block-spans with tokens being tokens, opener being index, upto being upto
            when spans.0 is less than 0 then
                give failed-render with complaint being "a <% " plus kind plus " %> has no <% end %>"
            end when
            value held is is-set with page-data being page-data, name being token.body
            value taken is when kind equals "if" give held otherwise give not held end when
            value branch is when taken
                give (render-range with tokens being tokens, start-at being index plus 1,
                    upto being (when spans.1 is at least 0 give spans.1 otherwise give spans.0 end when),
                    page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth)
                otherwise give (render-else with tokens being tokens, spans being spans,
                    page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth)
            end when
            when not branch.rendered then
                give branch
            end when
            set out to out plus branch.text-out
            set index to spans.0 plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "loop" then
            value spans is block-spans with tokens being tokens, opener being index, upto being upto
            when spans.0 is less than 0 then
                give failed-render with complaint being "a <% for %> has no <% end %>"
            end when
            value repeated is render-loop with tokens being tokens, header being token.body,
                start-at being index plus 1, upto being spans.0, page-data being page-data,
                root being root, depth being depth
            when not repeated.rendered then
                give repeated
            end when
            set out to out plus repeated.text-out
            set index to spans.0 plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "else" or kind equals "ending" then
            give failed-render with complaint being "a <% " plus
                (when kind equals "ending" give "end" otherwise give "else" end when)
                plus " %> has no block to close"
        otherwise
            give failed-render with complaint being "unrecognised tag: <% " plus token.body plus " %>"
        end when
    end repeat
    give build render-result with text-out being out, rendered being true, complaint being ""
end paragraph


render-else receives tokens as array of template-token, spans as tuple of (number, number),
    page-data as render-context, root as text, depth as number returns render-result begin paragraph
    when spans.1 is less than 0 then
        give build render-result with text-out being "", rendered being true, complaint being ""
    end when
    give render-range with tokens being tokens, start-at being spans.1 plus 1, upto being spans.0,
        page-data being page-data, root being root, depth being depth
end paragraph


!!! --- Find a block's `end`, and its `else` if it has one at this level.
!!!
!!! Gives back (end-index, else-index), each minus one when absent. Nested
!!! blocks are counted so an inner `end` does not close an outer block, and an
!!! `else` inside a nested block is not mistaken for this one's.

block-spans receives tokens as array of template-token, opener as number, upto as number
    returns tuple of (number, number) begin paragraph
    variable nesting as number is 0
    variable else-at as number is 0 minus 1
    variable index as number is opener plus 1
    repeat while index is less than upto
        value kind is (tokens at index).kind
        when kind equals "if" or kind equals "unless" or kind equals "loop" then
            set nesting to nesting plus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "ending" then
            when nesting equals 0 then
                give (index, else-at)
            end when
            set nesting to nesting minus 1
        otherwise when kind equals "else" and nesting equals 0 and else-at is less than 0 then
            set else-at to index
        end when
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give (0 minus 1, else-at)
end paragraph


!!! --- `<% for one in many %>`: render the body once per row of `many`, with
!!! each row's cells bound under `one`.
!!!
!!! A set with no rows renders nothing, which is what an empty list should
!!! look like. A header that is not `<name> in <name>` is a template bug and
!!! says so rather than quietly rendering zero times.

render-loop receives tokens as array of template-token, header as text, start-at as number, upto as number,
    page-data as render-context, root as text, depth as number returns render-result begin paragraph
    value binder is nil.std.text::trim with s being (before-first with input being header, separator being " in ")
    value source-name is nil.std.text::trim with s being (after-first with input being header, separator being " in ")
    when binder equals "" or source-name equals "" then
        give failed-render with complaint being "a <% for %> needs '<one> in <many>', found: " plus header
    end when

    value rows is rows-of with page-data being page-data, name being source-name
    variable out as text is ""
    variable position as number is 0
    repeat for each one-row in rows
        variable inner is with-row-bound with page-data being page-data, prefix being binder, one-row being one-row
        set inner to with-number with page-data being inner, name being binder plus ".index", amount being position
        set inner to with-flag with page-data being inner, name being binder plus ".first",
            held being position equals 0
        set inner to with-flag with page-data being inner, name being binder plus ".last",
            held being position equals (the length of rows) minus 1
        value piece is render-range with tokens being tokens, start-at being start-at, upto being upto,
            page-data being inner, root being root, depth being depth
        when not piece.rendered then
            give piece
        end when
        set out to out plus piece.text-out
        set position to position plus 1
    end repeat
    give build render-result with text-out being out, rendered being true, complaint being ""
end paragraph


!!! --- Load a template start-at under `root`.
!!!
!!! The name must stay inside the template directory. A name containing `..`
!!! is refused outright rather than resolved and checked afterwards: the
!!! check-after-resolve shape is the one that goes wrong on the platform
!!! nobody tested, and a template name has no legitimate reason to climb.

public load-template receives name as text, root as text returns render-result begin paragraph
    value guarded is guard-name with name being name
    when not (guarded equals "") then
        give failed-render with complaint being guarded
    end when

    value path is when root equals "" give name otherwise give root plus "/" plus name end when
    when not (nil.std.io::exists with path being path) then
        give failed-render with complaint being "no such template: " plus name
    end when
    value outcome is nil.std.io::read_text with path being path
    consider outcome
        when Result.Ok holding body then
            give build render-result with text-out being body, rendered being true, complaint being ""
        when Result.Error holding why then
            give failed-render with complaint being "could not read template " plus name plus ": " plus why
        otherwise
            give failed-render with complaint being "could not read template " plus name
    end consider
end paragraph


!!! --- Whether a template name is allowed, as a complaint or "" for allowed.
!!!
!!! Refused by shape rather than resolved and then checked. The
!!! check-after-resolve shape is the one that goes wrong on the platform
!!! nobody tested, and a template name has no legitimate reason to climb.

guard-name receives name as text returns text begin paragraph
    when name equals "" then
        give "a template was asked for by an empty name"
    end when
    when nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being ".." then
        give "a template name may not climb out of the template directory: " plus name
    end when
    when (nil.std.text::starts_with with s being name, prefix being "/")
        or (nil.std.text::contains with s being name, needle being ":") then
        give "a template name must be relative: " plus name
    end when
    give ""
end paragraph


failed-render receives complaint as text returns render-result begin paragraph
    give build render-result with text-out being "", rendered being false, complaint being complaint
end paragraph
